name: Market Pullback Screen

Every trading day at 9:45am & 4:15pm , scan all companies in the Nasdaq-100 and the Dow Jones Industrial Average.

Rank stocks by Year-to-Date (YTD) performance.
Select the top 5 best-performing stocks from each index.
Remove any duplicate stocks that appear in both lists.
From the remaining stocks, identify only those that have declined at least 10% during the last 30 calendar days.
For each qualifying stock, provide:
Company name
Ticker symbol
Current stock price
YTD return (%)
30-day return (%)
Percentage below its 30-day high
Average daily trading volume
Market capitalization
Brief explanation (2–3 sentences) for the recent decline
Upcoming earnings date (if applicable)
Whether the stock still has a bullish long-term trend based on the 50-day and 200-day moving averages

Finally, rank the qualifying stocks from most attractive to least attractive as potential pullback opportunities, and explain the reasoning behind the ranking.
